# Why this file exists (#309, Vitest 5 migration).
#
# `@angular/build` declares `peerOptional vitest ^4.0.8` for its
# `@angular/build:unit-test` builder — a builder this repo configures in
# angular.json but NEVER invokes: all six `test:*` scripts call
# `vitest run --config projects/<p>/vitest.config.ts` directly. On Vitest 5 that
# stale optional peer makes a plain `npm install` (and `npm ls`) exit 1, which
# broke the documented onboarding command in README.md / README_TESTING.md.
#
# Every install path in this repo already passed `--legacy-peer-deps` explicitly
# (frontend/Dockerfile, frontend/Dockerfile.admin, all five `npm i` steps in
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml, bump_version.sh). This file makes that posture
# the project default instead of a flag each caller must remember, so the
# documented commands work as written.
#
# TRADE-OFF, stated honestly: this silences GENUINE peer conflicts too, not just
# this known-stale one. Mitigations we rely on instead: the lockfile is
# regenerated in one pass and reviewed programmatically on every dependency
# change (lessons-learned §14 and §45), and Dependabot still opens PRs that
# surface real upstream incompatibilities. Revisit — and delete this file — when
# `@angular/build` widens its `vitest` peer range past 4.x.
legacy-peer-deps=true
